#: package/datasets/Simulatedtwo-periodDiD.description
msgid ""
"2000 units observed before (2010) and after (2015) with trends that depend "
"on covariate x; true effect 1.5. Classic DiD (2x2) - outcome y, treated "
"group treated, period year, unit id id, covariates x and region."
msgstr ""

#: didiag/results/bacon.columns.title
msgid "2x2 comparisons"
msgstr "2×2比較の数"

#: package/datasets/CastleDoctrinelawsandhomicide(Cheng&Hoekstra).description
msgid ""
"50 US states 2000-2010; staggered adoption of castle doctrine laws, 29 "
"states never treated. Compare DiD Estimators or DiD Diagnostics - outcome "
"l_homicide, unit state, period year, treatment post (indicator) or effyear "
"(first treated period, 0 = never); covariates population, income, "
"unemployrt, poverty, police; weights pop2000 (population in 2000). Source - "
"bacondecomp package, from Cheng and Hoekstra (2013)."
msgstr ""

#: package/datasets/Minimumwageandteenemployment(mpdta,Callaway&Sant'Anna).description
msgid ""
"500 US counties 2003-2007, staggered minimum-wage increases. Compare DiD "
"Estimators - outcome lemp, unit countyreal, period year, treatment "
"first.treat with type First treated period (0 = never); covariate lpop. "
"Source - did package."
msgstr ""

#: package/datasets/Simulatedstaggeredadoption.description
msgid ""
"600 units, 12 periods, three treatment cohorts with growing effects, so TWFE "
"is biased (true average effect on the treated about 1.7). Compare DiD "
"Estimators or DiD Diagnostics - outcome y, unit id, period year, treatment D "
"(indicator) or g (first treated period)."
msgstr ""

#: package/datasets/Simulatedtripledifferences.description
msgid ""
"800 units in treated and untreated groups with a group-wide shock that also "
"hits ineligible units; true effect on eligible units about 1.49. Triple "
"Differences (DDD) - outcome y, unit id, period year, first treated period g, "
"eligibility elig."
msgstr ""

#: package/datasets/Simulatedcontinuoustreatment.description
msgid ""
"800 units, 4 periods, dose between 0.1 and 1 for treated units; the effect "
"of dose d is 2d plus d squared. Continuous Treatment DiD - outcome y, unit "
"id, period year, first treated period g, dose dose."
msgstr ""

